  m_text: In this stage, the plant absorbs carbon dioxide from the air through tiny
    openings in the leaves and water from the soil through its roots. Using the energy
    produced in the first stage, carbon dioxide is converted into glucose during
    the Calvin cycle. This stage does not require direct sunlight but depends on
    the energy formed earlier.
